    "result": "The vault's filesystem scaffold is in place, and `index.md` is byte-identical to before (SHA-256 `6b6b926e…4215`, checked before and after). I did not touch the app, publication or the plugin.\n\n**Filesystem initialization**\n- **Preflight:** the vault held only `index.md`. There was no `AGENTS.md` and no `_templates/`, so there were no template collisions and `init.mjs` was safe to run.\n- **Operation:** I opened operation `530d9d9bec7d458f` (`relink`) before scaffolding. `init.mjs` exited 0.\n- **Files created:**\n  - Root files: `.gitignore`, `log.md`, `vault-schema.md`, `stale.base` and `log.base`.\n  - Six templates in `_templates/`.\n  - Folders: `raw/clippings/`, `wiki/{sources,entities,concepts,syntheses,authored}/`, `moc/` and `log/`.\n- **Ledger:** `init.mjs` doesn't record files itself, so I added the 11 new files by hand. With the log entry `log/2026-11-02-155756-relink-initialize-vault.md`, the ledger holds 12 paths.\n- **Health:** status is `empty`, with 0 defects and 0 content pages scanned. This shows the structure is sound, not that any content is factually healthy. The ingest backlog is 0 in every category.\n- **Operation close:** `op-commit.mjs` exited 0 but reported \"not a git repository — nothing to commit\". I did not create a repository. The `.wiki-master/ops` directory is empty now, so the token appears to be closed.\n\n**App integration (not done, not authorized)**\n- You still need to open the folder as an Obsidian vault and check it with `obsidian.mjs vaults`.\n- You still need to import `templates/webclipper-template.json` into Web Clipper.\n- The native CLI's access to the app is untested.\n\n**Publication**\n- The vault is local-only: there is no Git repository, no commit and no remote, and nothing was published.\n- Semantic search isn't built yet. Running `index-embed.mjs` would enable it, but I didn't run it because it wasn't requested.",
